<!-- ══ WHAT IS A CALC SOLVER ══ -->
<section class="home-section" id="calc-solver">
  <div class="section-header">
    <h2 class="section-title">What Is a Calc Solver?</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">A calculator that shows you how, not just what</p>
  </div>
  <div class="home-prose">
    <p>A calc solver is simply a calculator you can lean on when a sum gets awkward. You type in the problem, it gives you the answer, and the better ones also show the working so you can see where the answer came from. That is what we try to do here. The scientific calculator above handles everything from a quick 15% tip to sine, cosine and logarithms, and the 15 solvers below it each focus on one kind of homework question.</p>
    <p>People find tools like this under lots of different names: calc solver, calcsolver, solve calc, solvecalc, solver calc, online scientific calculator. Whatever you typed to get here, the idea is the same. You need a fast, free calculator that works on a school Chromebook, a phone or a laptop, with no download and no account.</p>
    <p>We would rather you understand a method than copy an answer, so most tools show the steps. If you are checking homework, work the problem on paper first, then use the solver to confirm it. If your answers do not match, the steps tell you exactly which line to look at again.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══ HOW TO USE THE CALCULATOR ══ -->
<section class="home-section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <h2 class="section-title">How to Use the Scientific Calculator</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Four quick habits that prevent most mistakes</p>
  </div>
  <div class="how-grid">
    <div class="how-card">
      <div class="how-num">1</div>
      <div class="how-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-keyboard"></i></div>
      <h3 class="how-title">Type it the way it is written</h3>
      <p class="how-desc">Tap the keys or use your keyboard: digits, + - * /, Enter for equals, Backspace to delete and Esc to clear.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="how-card">
      <div class="how-num">2</div>
      <div class="how-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-list-ol"></i></div>
      <h3 class="how-title">Use brackets for order</h3>
      <p class="how-desc">The calculator follows the order of operations, so put ( ) around anything that must be worked out first, like (3 + 5) x 2.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="how-card">
      <div class="how-num">3</div>
      <div class="how-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-wave-square"></i></div>
      <h3 class="how-title">Trig works in degrees</h3>
      <p class="how-desc">sin, cos and tan expect degrees, and sin&#8315;&#185;, cos&#8315;&#185; and tan&#8315;&#185; give angles back in degrees. Check that this matches your question.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="how-card">
      <div class="how-num">4</div>
      <div class="how-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-rotate-left"></i></div>
      <h3 class="how-title">Replay to fix, don't retype</h3>
      <p class="how-desc">Made a typo in a long expression? Press Replay to bring it back, edit the part that is wrong and run it again.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

