<!-- ══ WORKED EXAMPLES ══ -->
<section class="home-section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <h2 class="section-title">Worked Examples You Can Try Right Now</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Type these into the calculator above and check you get the same answers</p>
  </div>
  <div class="ex-grid">
    <article class="ex-card">
      <h3>A percentage of an amount</h3>
      <p class="ex-q">What is 15% of 80?</p>
      <p>Turn 15% into 0.15, then multiply: 0.15 x 80 = <strong>12</strong>. The same method works for sale prices and tips.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="ex-card">
      <h3>Adding fractions</h3>
      <p class="ex-q">What is 3/4 + 2/3?</p>
      <p>Find a common denominator, 12. Then 9/12 + 8/12 = 17/12, which is <strong>1 5/12</strong> as a mixed number.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="ex-card">
      <h3>A one-step equation</h3>
      <p class="ex-q">Solve 2x + 5 = 17.</p>
      <p>Take 5 from both sides to get 2x = 12, then divide both sides by 2. So <strong>x = 6</strong>. Check it: 2 x 6 + 5 = 17.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="ex-card">
      <h3>The area of a circle</h3>
      <p class="ex-q">A circle has radius 5. What is its area?</p>
      <p>Area = &#960; x r&#178; = &#960; x 25 = <strong>78.54</strong> square units, to two decimal places. Use the &#960; key, not 3.14, for a more exact answer.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="ex-card">
      <h3>A quadratic equation</h3>
      <p class="ex-q">Solve x&#178; - 5x + 6 = 0.</p>
      <p>Look for two numbers that multiply to 6 and add to -5: they are -2 and -3. So (x - 2)(x - 3) = 0 and <strong>x = 2 or x = 3</strong>.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="ex-card">
      <h3>The average of a list</h3>
      <p class="ex-q">Find the mean of 4, 6, 8, 10 and 12.</p>
      <p>Add them up to get 40, then divide by how many numbers there are: 40 / 5 = <strong>8</strong>. The median, the middle value, is also 8.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
